************ ADDITIONAL EXPERIMENT: 1 ************
SELECTION SORT

AIM:
To sort an array of integers in ascending order using Selection Sort.

ALGORITHM:

1. Declare and initialize an integer array.
2. Find the minimum element in the unsorted portion of the array.
3. Compare the elements and identify the smallest value.
4. Swap the smallest element with the first element of the unsorted portion.
5. Repeat the process until the array is sorted.
6. Display the sorted array.

---

************ ADDITIONAL EXPERIMENT: 2 ************
ABSTRACT CLASS

AIM:
To calculate the areas of Circle, Rectangle and Triangle using an abstract class.

ALGORITHM:

1. Create an abstract class Shape with two integer variables and an abstract method printArea().
2. Create Circle, Rectangle and Triangle subclasses that extend Shape.
3. Override printArea() in each subclass.
4. Calculate the circle area using π × radius × radius.
5. Calculate the rectangle area using length × width and the triangle area using ½ × base × height.
6. Create objects of all three subclasses and display their areas.

